{"id":"claim:nominal/nominal-derivation-diminutive-augmentative--the-suffix-po-originated-as-a-diminutive-suffix","revision":1,"topic":"topic:nominal/nominal-derivation-diminutive-augmentative","topics":["topic:nominal/nominal-derivation-diminutive-augmentative","topic:nominal/nominal-derivation-diminutive-augmentative--horobetsu"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -po originated as a diminutive suffix meaning 'child', used for 'small thing' or 'cute thing'; ak-po is allowed only in epic poetry, whereas in colloquial Horobetsu speech attaching -po to loved ones means 'deceased'.","ja":"接尾辞-poは元来「子」に発した指小辞で「小さいもの」「可愛いもの」等を意味するが、ak-poは叙事詩にのみ許される形であり、幌別地方の口語で-poを親しいものに付けると「死んだ（故人）」の意になる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-po","ak-po","ku-aki-po","ku-kor oper-po"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0039-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
